            <title>[LU-21196] sanity test_27xt: truncate hangs in lov_layout_wait behind flusher fsync to a stopped OST</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21196</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_27xt (added by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20211" title="FLR-ECRO: allow 'truncate(file, 0)' and 'open(file, O_TRUNC)' on degraded EC file" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20211"&gt;LU-20211&lt;/a&gt;, "truncate(0) replaces layouts on stopped OST") timed out on review-ldiskfs-arm (rocky9.8 aarch64 clients, 64k pages) after the test stopped OST0 with its dirty plain-file page kept.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test set: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/de2802e5-f834-4503-806b-b886f4d4e630" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/de2802e5-f834-4503-806b-b886f4d4e630&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hang on the client (onyx-180vm6): the test's truncate(file, 0) sleeps in lov_layout_wait() via ll_layout_refresh() -&amp;gt; lov_conf_set(), waiting for lo_active_ios to drop to 0. At the same time the flusher kworker (wb_workfn -&amp;gt; ll_writepages -&amp;gt; cl_sync_file_range) is blocked for the whole 118 minutes in wait_for_completion() in osc_io_fsync_end(), holding the active IO against the stopped OST, so neither finishes. The test clears OBD_FAIL_OSC_NO_FLUSH before the truncate, and stopping the OST took about 40 s on this arm cluster (00:03:43 to 00:04:20), long enough for periodic writeback to start on the kept dirty page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Frequency: 1 failure in 24 review-ldiskfs-arm runs, 0 in 136 review-ldiskfs, and 0 in the other review configs, so a timing race rather than a config problem. Not related to the tests: unmount in parallel change (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17240" title="change test-framework to format and mount targets in parallel " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17240"&gt;LU-17240&lt;/a&gt;, change 63189): the test only calls stop() once, serially.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suspects: the layout change should not wait on an fsync that cannot complete against an unavailable OST (the code under &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20211" title="FLR-ECRO: allow 'truncate(file, 0)' and 'open(file, O_TRUNC)' on degraded EC file" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20211"&gt;LU-20211&lt;/a&gt;), or the test's dirty-page hold is not robust against flusher writeback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-63189-ps7-73a3cd8e463d on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/63189" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/63189&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
